> does 2x + 3 overflow for a signed byte x?
  ucas: it(x: i8) = 2*x + 3
  ucas: wrap it
wrap analysis of it:
  2x   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  2x + 3   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 2 points, e.g. x=-1
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 2 points, e.g. x=-65  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      exact for: -65..62
  over all 256 points of the domain
