  searched [-10, 10] (default; give x a range)
> where is x cubed minus 3x increasing?
  ucas: it(x) = x^3 - 3*x
  ucas: monotonic it
monotonic it:
  not monotonic on all real x
  maximal intervals of monotonicity:
    x in (-inf, -1]: increasing
    x in [-1, 1]: decreasing
    x in [1, inf): increasing
  witness: x = -2 < x = -1 but f(-2) = -2 < f(-1) = 2 (not decreasing)
  witness: x = -1 < x = 1 but f(-1) = 2 > f(1) = -2 (not increasing)
  proved symbolically: it' = 3x^2 - 3; its real roots: -1, 1 (exact); f' keeps its sign between roots of odd multiplicity
> where is x cubed minus 3x decreasing?
  ucas: it(x) = x^3 - 3*x
  ucas: monotonic it
monotonic it:
  not monotonic on all real x
  maximal intervals of monotonicity:
    x in (-inf, -1]: increasing
    x in [-1, 1]: decreasing
    x in [1, inf): increasing
  witness: x = -2 < x = -1 but f(-2) = -2 < f(-1) = 2 (not decreasing)
  witness: x = -1 < x = 1 but f(-1) = 2 > f(1) = -2 (not increasing)
  proved symbolically: it' = 3x^2 - 3; its real roots: -1, 1 (exact); f' keeps its sign between roots of odd multiplicity
