> the 5th roots of unity
  ucas: unity 5
the 5 fifth roots of 1 (w^5 = 1)
  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)
  w1 = (-1 + sqrt(5))/4 + i*sqrt((5 + sqrt(5))/8) = e^(i*2pi/5)
  w2 = -(1 + sqrt(5))/4 + i*sqrt((5 - sqrt(5))/8) = e^(i*4pi/5)
  w3 = -(1 + sqrt(5))/4 - i*sqrt((5 - sqrt(5))/8) = e^(-i*4pi/5)
  w4 = (-1 + sqrt(5))/4 - i*sqrt((5 + sqrt(5))/8) = e^(-i*2pi/5)
  check: each w^5, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically
