> the fourier series of a square wave on -1 to 1
  ucas: fourier series sign(x) on -1 to 1
Fourier series of sign(x) on [-1, 1] (period 2):
  f(x) ~ a0/2 + sum_{n>=1} a_n cos(pi*n*x) + b_n sin(pi*n*x)
  a_n = int f(x) cos(pi*n*x) dx over the period, b_n likewise with sin
  a0 = 0
  a_n = 0 (f is odd)
  b_n = 2(1 - (-1)^n)/(pi*n)
  check: the closed forms equal the numeric coefficients (Gauss-Legendre, 5120 nodes) for n = 1..48
  f(x) ~ 4sin(pi*x)/pi + 4sin(3pi*x)/(3pi) + 4sin(5pi*x)/(5pi) + 4sin(7pi*x)/(7pi) + 4sin(9pi*x)/(9pi) + ...
  partial sums S_N: ||f - S_N||/||f|| = 0.259 (N = 5), 0.0919 (N = 48)
  converges to f where f is continuous, and to the midpoint of the jump where it jumps:
    at x = 0 it jumps by 2: S_N -> 0
    at x = 1 it jumps by -2: S_N -> the midpoint
  Gibbs: near x = 0, S_48 overshoots by 0.1791 = 9.0% of the jump (at x = 0.02083); the overshoot tends to 8.95% of the jump and does not shrink as N grows
